@page "/docs/direction"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Direction
<PageTitle>Direction (RTL) - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Direction (RTL)</h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">Blaizio components follow the reading direction. Set it globally with <code>dir</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, or scope it to a region with <code>DirectionProvider</code> - the styling mirrors (logical CSS properties) and keyboard navigation swaps left/right in step. The examples below use Arabic copy; try the LTR/RTL switch in the top bar to flip this whole site.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(DirectionUsageExample)"
                Description="Wrap any subtree in a DirectionProvider; everything inside follows that reading direction. Spacing, alignment and arrow-key navigation all mirror." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Scoped to a subtree" Description="A DirectionProvider flips just its children - icon side, text alignment, tab order and arrow keys all mirror, while the rest of the page stays as it is."
          Example="typeof(DirectionScopedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Per-component override" Description="A dir attribute on any single component overrides the ambient direction for just that component."
          Example="typeof(DirectionPerComponentExample)" />

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">How it works</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Direction is expressed as the standard <code>dir</code> attribute in the DOM. <code>DirectionProvider</code> sets it on a layout-neutral wrapper for its subtree, so two things follow from one place: CSS logical properties (paddings, borders, alignment) mirror, and the JS that drives roving-focus arrow keys reads the live direction and swaps Left/Right. Equivalently you can put a raw <code>dir="rtl"</code> on any component, or - on a headless primitive - pass <code>Dir="Direction.Rtl"</code>.</p>
    </section>
    <ApiReference Types="ApiFamilies.DirectionProvider" />
</div>

